{
  "name": "Build a searchable PDF knowledge base from Google Drive: OCR, Markdown, embed, and chat with citations",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Build a searchable PDF knowledge base from Google Drive: OCR, Markdown, embed, and chat with citations\n\n**Community node.** This template uses the pdfRest API Toolkit community node (@pdfrest/n8n-nodes-pdfrest), so it runs on self-hosted n8n only. Install it under Settings > Community Nodes before importing.\n\n### Who it's for\nTeams with a Drive folder of PDFs \u2014 policies, manuals, contracts, research \u2014 who want to ask questions across all of them and get answers that cite the source document and page.\n\n### How it works\n**Ingest (top row)**\n1. The Google Drive Trigger watches a Knowledge folder for new PDFs and downloads each one.\n2. pdfRest **Extract \u00b7 Query PDF Info** reads page count and whether the file is image-only.\n3. Image-only scans go through pdfRest **Extract \u00b7 OCR PDF**; born-digital PDFs skip it.\n4. pdfRest **Convert \u00b7 PDF to Markdown** returns clean text with page-break comments.\n5. A Code node splits the Markdown on page breaks so every chunk carries its page number and file name as metadata.\n6. A Recursive Character Text Splitter and an embeddings model load the chunks into a vector store.\n7. Google Sheets records the file, page count, chunk count, and ingest time.\n\n**Chat (bottom row)**\n8. The Chat Trigger accepts a question. An AI Agent uses the vector store as a tool, retrieves the most relevant chunks, and answers with the file name and page for each fact it uses.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Install the pdfRest community node and add a pdfRest API credential.\n2. Connect Google Drive, Google Sheets, an embeddings credential (Google Gemini shown), and a chat model credential (Anthropic shown).\n3. In **Configuration**, paste the manifest Sheet ID and set the OCR language.\n4. In **Watch Knowledge Folder**, pick the Drive folder to index.\n5. Create the manifest Sheet with headers: Ingested, File, Pages, Chunks, OCR Applied, Drive Link.\n6. Drop a few PDFs in the folder, wait for ingest, then open the chat and ask a question.\n\n### Requirements\nSelf-hosted n8n, the pdfRest community node, a pdfRest API key, Google Drive, Google Sheets, an embeddings provider key, and a chat model key.\n\n### How to customize\nReplace the Simple Vector Store with Pinecone, Qdrant, Supabase, or PGVector for a persistent index \u2014 the Simple Vector Store resets when n8n restarts. Swap Gemini embeddings for OpenAI, Cohere, Mistral, or Ollama. Change the agent's system message to enforce your citation format or restrict it to the knowledge base only. Add pdfRest **Convert \u00b7 PDF to PDF/A** before upload to keep an archival copy alongside the index.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1180,
        "color": 1
      },
